$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Hydroxyamide Derivatives. General
Procedure A.29 To a stirring solution of amine (1 mmol) in EtOH at rt,
the carboxylic acid (1.03 mmol), NMM (2.2 mmol), and HOBt (0.15 mmol)
were subsequently added. The solution was then cooled to 0 °C, and EDC
(1.2 mmol) was added. The reaction was stirred at rt overnight, followed
by the addition of 0.1 M citric acid. The mixture was then extracted with
EtOAc (3×). The combined organic phases were washed with brine (1×),
dried over anhydrous MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
crude material was purified by column chromatography to give the
indicated product. N-Boc-Ser(Bn)-Ser-OMe (12). Following general
procedure A on a 5.57 mmol scale of HCl·Ser-OMe using Boc-Ser(OBn)-OH
(1.70 g, 5.74 mmol), EDC (1.29 g, 6.69 mmol), NMM (1.35 mL, 12.25 mmol),
and HOBt (112.93 mg, 0.84 mmol) in EtOH (20 mL). N-Boc-Cys(Tr)-Ser-OMe
(14). Following general procedure A on a 3.15 mmol scale of HCl·Ser-OMe
using Boc-Cys(Tr)-OH (1.50 g, 3.25 mmol), EDC (742.32 mg, 3.78 mmol), NMM
(762 μL, 6.93 mmol), and HOBt (65.20 mg, 0.47 mmol) in EtOH (20 mL). The
desired product (1.59 g, 2.81 mmol, 89%) was isolated as a white solid by
silica gel column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc, 3:1). Rf (hexane/EtOAc,
1:1) 0.43; IR (neat) ν = 3392, 3319, 3055, 2974, 2358, 2335, 1745, 1671,
1491, 1444, 1391, 1367, 1248, 1166, 1030, 861, 743, 701, 627 cm-1; 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.29-7.21 (m, 15H), 6.79 (d, J = 8.1, 1H), 4.77 (d, J
= 5.7, 1H), 4.76-4.54 (m, 1H), 4.03 (dd, J 1 = 2.7, J 2 = 9.9, 1H), 3.94
(m, 1H), 3.76 (dd, J 1 = 3.0, J 2 = 10.1, 1H), 3.69 (s, 3H), 2.78 (dd, J
1 = 5.7, J 2 = 13.2, 1H), 2.54 (dd, J 1 = 4.8, J 2 = 12.6, 1H), 1.42 (s,
9H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 170.8, 170.6, 144.5, 129.8, 128.4, 128.3,
127.2, 80.3, 67.5, 62.7, 55.3, 54.2, 52.9, 34.2, 28.5; HRMS (ESI-TOF)
m/z: [M + Na]+ calculated for C31H36N2O6SNa 587.2186, found 587.2189.
