$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure E for the Preparation of
Benzanilide Substrates: In a scintillation vial equipped with a stir bar
was combined the amine (0.15 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and the di-Boc protected
acid coupling partner (0.10 g, 0.29 mmol, 2.0 equiv) in THF (0.50 mL,
0.30 M). EDCI hydrochloride (29 mg, 0.15 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was
subsequently added. The reaction progress was monitored by LC-MS.
Complete conversion of the amine starting material to product was
observed after approximately 1h. The solvent was removed under reduced
pressure, and the crude residue was then dissolved in a 1:1 mixture of
TFA:CH2Cl2 (4.0 mL total). After 1 h, the solvent was removed.
Purification by reverse-phase column chromatography (gradient: 10% MeCN
to 100% MeCN in H2O + 0.1% TFA) and subsequent lyophilization. The
products as TFA salts. Substrate 5a: The coupling of commercially
available benzylamine by procedure E. Substrate 18a: The coupling of
commercially available 3-phenyl benzylamine by procedure E. 18a in 82%
yield. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD d-4): δ 7.62-7.29 (m, 9H), 4.44 (s, 2H),
3.22 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 2.36 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 1.89 (quin, J = 7.2
Hz, 2H). 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CD3OD): δ 174.92, 158.76, 142.86, 142.27,
140.58, 130.10, 129.86, 128.45, 127.99, 127.54, 127.29, 126.95, 44.22,
41.89, 33.25, 25.99. HRMS (For C18H23N4O, MH+): Calc’d 311.1872, found
311.1873.
